UNBOUND ALIAS ARMS OF `parse_ec_dimension_kind`, WHERE FAILURE DELETES THE ITEM. Rule: capability.rs:11705-11716 accepts `behaviour`/`functional`/`function`/`render` as `behavior`, `performance`/`perf` as `efficiency`, and `secure` as `security`; `is_ec_dimension_contract_key` (capability.rs:11409-11411) is defined as `parse_ec_dimension_kind(value).is_some()`, and `parse_capability_ec_dimensions` (capability.rs:11322) propagates None through a `filter_map` `?`, so an unrecognized spelling does not fall back -- it silently DROPS the whole EC dimension. Mutation M192 (verbatim): replace `        "behavior" | "behaviour" | "functional" | "function" | "render" => {
            Some(CapabilityEcDimensionKind::Behavior)
        }
        "efficiency" | "performance" | "perf" => Some(CapabilityEcDimensionKind::Efficiency),
        "security" | "secure" => Some(CapabilityEcDimensionKind::Security),` with the canonical-only arms `        "behavior" => {
            Some(CapabilityEcDimensionKind::Behavior)
        }
        "efficiency" => Some(CapabilityEcDimensionKind::Efficiency),
        "security" => Some(CapabilityEcDimensionKind::Security),`. Verdict: SURVIVED at gate exit 0. Why the fixture cannot observe it: MEMBER_EC_DIMENSION (lumen_feature_class_reference.py:366-374) uses only the four canonical spellings, and the import-time assert at 375-380 pins coverage of the enum rather than of the spellings that reach it. Reachability confirmed: a capability declaring `- behaviour: ...` and `- perf: ...` migrates at exit 0 into `- behavior: ...` and `- efficiency: ...` (probe A). Under the mutant that same input renders an `EC Dimensions:` field with zero items -- the author's declared dimensions are gone, and every downstream production gate that requires a dimension is satisfied by a document the product itself rewrote. This is a false green of the #694 class on authored input. Revision: declare one capability whose EC dimension uses `perf` and another using `behaviour`, and assert the rendered item list is exactly the canonicalized pair -- as an exact item list, not a containment, so the dropped-item failure mode is observable.

