        || capability.gaps.iter().all(|gap| {
            matches!(
                gap.status,
                CapabilityGapStatus::Closed | CapabilityGapStatus::Deferred
            )
        })
    {` with `    if capability.status == CapabilityStatus::Verified
        || false
    {`. Verdict: SURVIVED at gate exit 0. Why the fixture cannot observe it: on every document where the Index Impl column is asserted, the capability's status is already `Verified`, so the first disjunct answers and the second is never the deciding one. Reachability confirmed: a `candidate` capability whose single work root is `implemented | verified` renders Impl `implemented` in the Capability Index against the unmutated binary (probe A), and a `candidate` with no work-root table at all renders `implemented` through the vacuous-`all` path (probe E) -- both become `planned` under the mutant. Revision: on the varied-status document, declare a non-`verified` capability whose work-root rows are all closed and assert its Index Impl cell is `implemented`, beside an existing non-verified capability with an in-progress row asserted `partial`, so the two disjuncts are separated.

